From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camel: allow a prebuilt camel-gen-tables

camel-gen-tables is compiled as a target executable and then run during
the build to generate camel-mime-tables.c. That only works where the
build and target architectures agree. Cross compiling to aarch64 on an
x86_64 builder stops here:

  aarch64-binfmt-P: Could not open '/lib/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1': No such
    file or directory
  make[3]: *** [src/camel/camel-mime-tables.c] Error 255

This is the same shape as gen-western-table, which already takes
-DGEN_WESTERN_TABLE=, so give camel-gen-tables the same treatment:
name a ready-made one with -DCAMEL_GEN_TABLES= and the target
executable is not built at all. Without it, nothing changes.

The generator needs no libraries - stdio and the configured header -
so building one for the build machine is a single compile.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/src/camel/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/camel/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -10,18 +10,36 @@
 	camel-url.h
 )
 
-add_executable(camel-gen-tables
-	camel-gen-tables.c
-)
+# camel-gen-tables runs during the build to produce camel-mime-tables.c, so it
+# has to be a program of the build machine. Building it as a target executable
+# only works where the two architectures happen to agree; cross compiling to
+# aarch64 on an x86_64 builder stops here instead:
+#
+#   aarch64-binfmt-P: Could not open '/lib/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1'
+#
+# Accept a ready-made one through CAMEL_GEN_TABLES. When it is not given
+# nothing changes. It needs no libraries - stdio and the configured header -
+# so building one for the host is a single compile.
+if(CAMEL_GEN_TABLES)
+	set(_camel_gen_tables_exe ${CAMEL_GEN_TABLES})
+	set(_camel_gen_tables_dep)
+else(CAMEL_GEN_TABLES)
+	add_executable(camel-gen-tables
+		camel-gen-tables.c
+	)
 
-target_include_directories(camel-gen-tables PUBLIC
-	${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}
-)
+	target_include_directories(camel-gen-tables PUBLIC
+		${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}
+	)
+
+	set(_camel_gen_tables_exe ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/camel-gen-tables)
+	set(_camel_gen_tables_dep camel-gen-tables)
+endif(CAMEL_GEN_TABLES)
 
 add_custom_command(
 	OUTPUT ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/camel-mime-tables.c
-	COMMAND ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/camel-gen-tables >${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/camel-mime-tables.c
-	DEPENDS camel-gen-tables
+	COMMAND ${_camel_gen_tables_exe} >${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/camel-mime-tables.c
+	DEPENDS ${_camel_gen_tables_dep}
 )
 
 set(SOURCES
